<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-09-16T05:01:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>OpenAI boss says world 'right to be afraid' but 'should trust' AI firms</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T00:59:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o--4686332c8f93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Sam Altman and other tech CEOs say there are incentives to limit advancements in AI, as fears grow over the threats it poses to humanity.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI app ads promoting 'objectification of women' banned by watchdog</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T05:00:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T23:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o--3f8309803edf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The ad regulator said it had "zero-tolerance" for ads promoting AI tools that could sexualise or objectify women.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pubs in England and Wales to allow digital ID apps to prove age</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gl6j53w19o#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T23:07:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gl6j53w19o--5a4264a30fd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gl6j53w19o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">New rules introduced on Tuesday mean establishments will be able to accept digital ID apps alongside physical documents.</summary></entry><entry><title>Valve's Steam Frame is excellent - but at over £1,000 is VR still too expensive?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8m1113ym1o#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:05:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8m1113ym1o--e3780432d3ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8m1113ym1o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC's Tom Gerken is hands-on with the latest virtual reality headset.</summary></entry><entry><title>What is AI, how does it work and why are some people concerned about it?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2l799gxjjpo#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T16:09:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2l799gxjjpo--7bb18b050612.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2l799gxjjpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">AI is transforming modern life, but not without worry for some that it may be abused or have an adverse environmental impact.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why are there concerns AI could threaten humanity, and how real are they?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:00:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno--8128fa4f3ef2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Existential fears about AI have once again reared their head - here's what you need to know.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump downplays warnings of AI risks, citing rivalry with China</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c7v48vp31mdo#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:49:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c7v48vp31mdo--405af91616a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c7v48vp31mdo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The US president said "negative forces" were airing concerns about "things that won't happen".</summary></entry><entry><title>Questions mount over what an AI 'slowdown' would look like</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzp47py48o#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:20:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzp47py48o--6e6573f8c1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzp47py48o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">While pacing AI development might sound like a quick fix, it is far from an easy solution.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI staff 'genuinely frightened' for humanity's future, ex-Anthropic researcher tells BBC</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1kx0gyje9wo#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T14:53:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1kx0gyje9wo--e2bc2fc4f2ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1kx0gyje9wo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">It comes as the AI firm's boss has called for the technology's development to be slowed down, citing "serious" risks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Anthropic boss Dario Amodei calls for AI development to slow down</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c14dpgm0rg4o#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T21:16:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c14dpgm0rg4o--b9d28eb17909.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c14dpgm0rg4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The call comes amid growing concerns that AI models may become able to inflict serious damage worldwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>PlayStation gambles with 18-rated Wolverine game - will it pay off?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy0zq2n9gggo#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T00:35:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy0zq2n9gggo--24757eea03ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy0zq2n9gggo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC's Tom Gerken plays the hotly anticipated superhero game from Spider-Man makers Insomniac.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK government rejects 'kill switch' idea for dangerous AI</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3eq7kl5l00o#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:07:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3eq7kl5l00o--dce7b0e81cdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3eq7kl5l00o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Cabinet Office, which leads on AI safety, says the UK "cannot simply turn AI off".</summary></entry><entry><title>Does this AI comic make you laugh?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c5yjk63ww1ro#0</id><updated>2026-09-16T04:59:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T12:49:30Z</published><link rel=